# Cursor Rules — AI Teaching Material System

## Non-Negotiable Rules

0. **Harness engineering default.** Do not rely on chat memory for recurring instructions. Define the artifact and success gate, read the local context harness, use project scripts/templates, verify with concrete checks, inspect outputs/screenshots/logs/data, and update durable docs/skills/memory when Adam explicitly asks.
1. **Slide engine is Huashu Design (HTML-first).** Not Gamma. HTML is the primary presentation format. No PPTX in the workflow. PDF is backup only.
2. **Classroom presentation:** HTML presenter (index.html) used directly in class — fullscreen, annotation tools, PDF download.
3. **Shared slide assets:** Every lesson's `slides/assets/` must have `slide-base.css` + `slide-base.js`. Copy from lesson-01. Do NOT inline common CSS or `revealNext` JS in individual slides.
3. **Language:** Vietnamese for instructions, Simplified Chinese for content, pinyin for pronunciation.
4. **Review gate:** Steps 1-8 automated. Steps 9-18 require teacher approval. No separate student version — teacher deck is the classroom material.
5. **Page mapping:** Source page mapping lives in the database only. Vocab and sample slides do NOT show source page footers.
6. **Student safety:** No teacher tips or answers in student materials.
7. **No AI-isms.** Direct, specific, practical, concise.
8. **Cross-tool sync.** When updating `.kiro/`, also update AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md.
9. **Slide filenames:** Sequentially numbered matching MANIFEST position (no gaps). Lesson 01: 01–56.
10. **你好 standalone vocab slide:** Removed. Appears only in vocab summary quiz and dialogue.
11. **Vocab counter:** Format `XX/YY`. Lesson 01 total = 11.
12. **Pinyin word grouping:** Pinyin of a multi-syllable word must be written together (no space between syllables of one word). Correct: "dìèr kè · nǐ shì nǎguó rén?" Wrong: "dì èr kè · nǐ shì nǎ guó rén?" Each vocabulary word's pinyin is one unit. Sentence pinyin groups by word boundaries.
13. **Image asset workflow:** Images are lesson data. VP databases carry `image_role`, `image_prompt`, `image_file`, `image_reuse_from`, `image_status`, and `image_semantic_check`. Complete lessons must have `slides/assets/asset-manifest.json` and `exports/qa/asset-qa-report.json`.
14. **Pinyin course (6 lessons):** Source is AI Mandarin independent material (`Pinyin lessons/`). Do NOT use 漢語教程 phonetics. Read `docs/pinyin-lesson-database-spec.md` for full spec. Pipeline config: `scripts/pipeline/configs/pinyin.json` v2.0.0. Output to `output/pinyin/pinyin-{01-06}/`.
15. **Pinyin Lesson 1 template baseline:** Future pinyin decks reuse `output/pinyin/pinyin-01`; do not build from scratch. Keep its cover/objectives/divider/concept/tone/vocab/flashcard/practice/input-setup/closing style, soft textbook/course images, and presenter behavior. Swap only lesson-specific text, sounds, rules, vocabulary, exercises, and images.
16. **Pinyin wording:** Use `thanh điệu`, never `thanh điều`. No `Mục lục` or `Quy ước` classroom slides. Pinyin slides do not show bottom-right `Trang ...` page indicators.

## Task Routing

| Task | Skill |
|------|-------|
| Any non-trivial task or repeated preference | `.kiro/skills/harness-engineering/SKILL.md` |
| Pipeline workflow, VP steps | `.kiro/skills/ai-teaching-material-systems/SKILL.md` |
| Pinyin lesson database or slide generation | `docs/pinyin-lesson-database-spec.md` |
| Slide design, HTML presenter, deck generation | `.kiro/skills/huashu-design/SKILL.md` |
| Google Drive/Sheets | `.kiro/skills/google-workspace/SKILL.md` |
| Writing quality | `.kiro/skills/avoid-ai-writing/SKILL.md` |

## HTML Presenter — required for every lesson

Every complete lesson's `slides/` folder must have `index.html`. Do not hand-edit copied presenter fields. After numbered slide HTML files exist, run `npm run lesson:presenter -- output/book-1/lesson-XX`, then `npm run lesson:shells`. Run `npm run lesson:shells` after database generation too, so draft lessons show a safe status page instead of redirecting to a missing presenter.

**Must include:** MANIFEST array, fullscreen (`F`), navigation, pen/highlighter/eraser/text-box annotation tools, on-demand PDF export (html2canvas + jsPDF — always current, no pre-baked data file).

**CDN deps (required in every index.html):**
```html
<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/jspdf/2.5.1/jspdf.umd.min.js"></script>
<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/html2canvas/1.4.1/html2canvas.min.js"></script>
```

**Do NOT use `slides-data.js`.** Deprecated.

## Reuse for new lessons

This system is reusable for any lesson or course type.

Generic slide scripts (all require `--slides-dir`):
- `node scripts/build-slides-data.mjs --slides-dir <path>`
- `node scripts/export-slides-pdf.mjs --slides-dir <path>`
- `node scripts/watch-slides.mjs --slides-dir <path>`

Image asset scripts:
- `npm run assets:manifest -- output/book-1/lesson-XX`
- `npm run assets:qa -- output/book-1/lesson-XX`
- `npm run assets:replace -- --lesson output/book-1/lesson-XX --record V001 --image /path/to/new.png`

Pipeline: `python scripts/run_pipeline.py --lesson-type regular|pinyin|auto --lesson-id <id> ...`

New lesson type: drop a JSON config in `scripts/pipeline/configs/` — no code changes needed.

Per-lesson fine-tuning is expected after initial slide generation. The system does not overwrite manual edits.
